data codex_bengalfox_rate_limit_id: NonEmptyStr = "codex_bengalfox" as NonEmptyStr
data codex_structured_error_code_rate_limit_reached: NonEmptyStr = "rate_limit_reached" as NonEmptyStr
data codex_structured_error_code_quota_exceeded: NonEmptyStr = "quota_exceeded" as NonEmptyStr
data codex_structured_error_code_authentication_required: NonEmptyStr = "authentication_required" as NonEmptyStr

data codex_rate_limits_capacity_decode_note: String = "GetAccountRateLimitsResponse carries rateLimits (backward-compatible single-bucket mirror) AND rateLimitsByLimitId (multi-bucket map keyed by limit_id, e.g. codex vs codex_bengalfox). Live exhausted Pro accounts can have codex at usedPercent 100 with rateLimitReachedType rate_limit_reached while another limit_id remains at 0 — a single account-level Ready|QuotaReached is therefore false. Decode every by-limit-id entry; keep native limit tokens open. spendControlReached true is an exhaustion signal when present, but live exhaustion often has spendControlReached false — usedPercent 100 and rateLimitReachedType are the operative facts. Empty rateLimits:\{\} answers the endpoint without proving capacity."

data codex_rate_limit_subject_encoding_note: String = "Standing bridge subject encoding (coord with gunbc.provider_standing / #7926, deep-raven-684 2026-08-06): each rateLimitsByLimitId entry projects to ProviderNativeLimitBucket \{ native_key: limit_id \} — NEVER ProviderAccountLimit. Promoting an exhausted codex bucket to account scope would block for the wrong reason, erase bucket identity, and wrongly refuse work that a sibling bucket (e.g. codex_bengalfox) could serve. If a truthful native-bucket observation does not block a dispatch that draws on that bucket, the defect is in limit_observation_blocks_selection coverage, not in this encoding. Discriminating control from the live capture: one inventory with codex at 100 percent and codex_bengalfox at 0 percent must refuse a dispatch that draws on codex and allow a dispatch that draws on codex_bengalfox."

data codex_model_to_limit_bucket_gap_note: String = "TYPED GAP — model → native limit_id is NOT observable on the 0.146 app-server surface. Model has no limitId; TurnStartParams.model is a free string with no bucket edge; RateLimitSnapshot carries limitId/limitName but no model join. Live limitName GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark on codex_bengalfox is suggestive folklore, not a cited join. dissolve-on: an upstream field or documented map that binds turn model (or service tier) to metered limit_id. Until then, consumers must not invent a closed mapping. The symbol codex_default_rate_limit_id names the backward-compatible rateLimits mirror's native key (live limitId=codex), which is the press AccountReady gate key — not a proven claim that every unspecified-model turn/start consumes that bucket."

